@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+---
+id: task-001-fix-three-order-service-bugs-lower-case-sku-lookup-free-shipping-threshold-vat-rounding
+type: task
+title: "Fix three order-service bugs: lower-case SKU lookup, free-shipping threshold, VAT rounding"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Reports handled
+
+1. Giulia (sales desk): a product code typed in lower case (e.g. `lb-220`) was refused as unknown,
+   while the same code in capitals worked.
+2. Marco (customer): a basket of exactly €50.00 after discount was still charged €4.90 delivery,
+   though the README states shipping is free from €50.00.
+3. Accounting: some order lines showed one cent less VAT than expected, e.g. €1.99 at the standard
+   rate (22%) showed €0.43 instead of €0.44.
+
+## Root causes and fixes
+
+1. `Catalog#find` (`src/catalog.ts`) looked products up by `sku.trim()` instead of the canonical form
+   (`canonicalSku`, which also upper-cases). A lower-case or mixed-case SKU therefore missed the map,
+   which stores products under their upper-case SKU. Fixed `find` to look up `canonicalSku(sku)`, which
+   also fixes `get`/`getForSale`, which call `find`.
+2. `shippingCost` (`src/shipping.ts`) waived shipping only when goods were strictly greater than
+   `FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS` (5000 cents), contradicting the README's "€50.00 or more". Changed the
+   comparison to `>=`.
+3. `lineVat` (`src/tax.ts`) rounded a line's VAT down (`Math.floor`) instead of half up to the cent, as
+   the README's money rules require (and as `percentOf`/`divideHalfUp` already do elsewhere). Changed
+   it to reuse `percentOf`, which rounds half up.
+
+## Tests
+
+Added one characterization test per bug (red before the fix, green after), following the red/green
+testing directive:
+
+- `test/catalog.test.ts`: looks a product up by a lower-case SKU.
+- `test/orders.test.ts`: an order whose goods are exactly €50.00 ships free.
+- `test/orders.test.ts`: a €1.99 line at the standard rate carries €0.44 VAT.
+
+`npm test` passes: 17/17.
+
+## Consequences
+
+No public API or behaviour beyond the three fixes changed. No migration needed: these are pure bug
+fixes bringing the code in line with the already-documented business rules in `README.md`.
